{
  "note": "Hand-written (phase 5 design 5.3, 4.5, 6.2; D135). A patient's current flags: currentFlags({changes, flags, hidden}) in packages/presets/src/current-flags.ts and apps/mobile/lib/presets/current_flags.dart; the readers are packages/presets/test/current-flags.test.ts and apps/mobile/test/presets/current_flags_test.dart, which run every case. `changes` are the flag changes of the patient's merged group, in the order they arrived (any order: the fold sorts them); `flags` are the team's flags by id, archived ones included, each with what the fold reads of it; `hidden` is the reader's flag rule, built by each reader from the case's `seesSensitive` as the server's flagHidden is for a flag of the team: hidden(flag) is flag.sensitive && !seesSensitive. The fold: a change marked entered in error is left out; so is a change whose flag is not among `flags`, and one whose flag `hidden` hides. The rest are ordered by effectiveAt, an instant (one written with an offset is that instant in UTC; milliseconds count), then by id, compared by UTF-16 code units. Primary: the primary-tier changes are folded in that order; a set makes its flag the primary; a clear makes the primary none only when its flag is the primary at that point, and otherwise changes nothing, so a clear of Medium from a phone that never saw High set takes nothing off. Secondary: a flag is carried when its own last change is a set; each carried flag once, ordered by rank, then by name compared by UTF-16 code units (JavaScript's < and Dart's compareTo), then by id. An archived flag is answered as any other: it stays on the patient, and can be cleared. The answer is {primary: a flag id or null, secondary: flag ids}. Every name, time and id here is made up.",
